-- MistressFlat3 (Fisherman Dad mistress, "Harbor" pink tower). Generated by build_flat_studio.py.
-- Studio, Edit mode. Usage (ModuleScript.Source = this file):
--   require(module)(flatJsonText, origin)
--     flatJsonText  text of data/flat.json
--     origin        Vector3 of the hidden flat origin (default -15000, 300, 15000: far away, never visible from the biome)
-- What it does:
--   1. Moves the imported FBX model Workspace.MistressFlat3 to the hidden origin (aligned by its bounding box, safe against pivot offsets).
--   2. Colours/materials (procedural, no images). Walls, floor, ceiling and window glass are solid for the camera (it cannot leave the flat).
--      The window view (group View, a lighter copy of the Harbor biome) is scenery only: no collision, no queries, no shadows.
--   3. Builds Workspace.FishermanMistressHarbor.MistressBuilding3:
--        Exterior: Entrance (tag ApartmentEntrance -> ApartmentService adds the «Войти» prompt and teleports) at the tower door, ExitArrival in front of it.
--        Interior: Meshes, Colliders, Lights, Arrival, ExitDoor (tag ApartmentExit), MistressSeat, GuestSeat,
--                  Table_Top (tag MistressDesk, DadId = "GardenerDad" = Fisherman Dad slot in DadCatalog).
--   ApartmentId is NOT set (owner decides). Re-run: delete MistressBuilding3.Interior, import the FBX again, run again.
